From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:48:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: Add Zinwa Q20 HD720 panel driver

Add a driver for the 720x720 two-lane video-mode DSI panel of the Zinwa
Q25. MediaTek's driver for it (panel-q20-hd720-lcm-dsi-vdo.c in the
LineageOS xelex_mt6789 kernel) sends no initialisation table on this
board, only sleep-out and display-on after a reset.

The panel has no brightness register (its DCS CTRL_DISPLAY reads 0): the
vendor kernel sets brightness by moving the source driver bias, codes
4.0 V + n x 0.1 V on the OCP2131. The driver registers a backlight device
with 21 levels that does the same through the AVDD/AVEE regulators, and
reads the starting level from the voltage the bootloader set.

The mode is the bootloader's, read back from the DSI registers it
programs: HSA 50, HBP 40, HFP 60, VSA 5, VBP 40 and VFP 68 on two lanes
at 652 Mbit/s, the link rate the panel needs to lock, which it asks for
through hs_rate. The panel runs at 70.93 Hz on it, measured from vblank
timestamps.

Unprepare sleeps the panel before it drops the bias; dropping the bias
under an awake panel leaves it ghosting.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
